# Build output.
/target

# Environment & keys.
#
# `.env` alone matched only that exact name, which is the rule that lets
# `.env.local` through — and this repository is public. Widened to the whole
# family, plus the shapes a key actually arrives in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Whole-repo dumps. Generated for tooling, and large enough that nobody reads
# what went into one before committing it.
CODEBASE_DUMP.txt

# Finder.
.DS_Store

# Screenshots and rendered sheets, which are generated and large.
#
# Golden images are the exception: they are the *specification* for a rendered
# view, they are reviewed in the diff like code, and a blanket `*.png` swallows
# them silently — they appear to work locally and are simply absent for everyone
# else. Any `tests/golden/` tree is therefore kept.
*.png
!**/tests/golden/**/*.png
# Screenshots the README actually shows. Same trap as the goldens: a blanket
# `*.png` swallows them silently, and a README whose image is missing looks
# worse than one with no image at all.
!assets/*.png

script.sh

# Working notes: the agent brief, the plans, the handoff, the devlog.
#
# Untracked deliberately — they are how this repository is *worked on* rather
# than what it is, and they carry session state (what is half-done, what was
# withdrawn) that goes stale the moment it is published. They stay on disk and
# stay useful; they are simply not part of what ships.
#
# Note for anyone reading this later: untracking does not remove them from the
# history. They are readable at every commit before this one.
#
# Keep README.md, CHANGELOG.md, CONTEXT.md, shipped Skills, and the Harness
# template in git. Those are the product.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
CODING_STANDARDS.md
HANDOFF.md
PLAN.md
LBR.md
NOTES.md
TODO.md
DEVLOG.md
session.md
docs/
.scratch/

# GH_Audit hygiene
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
target/
dist/
